sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Mitchison (1980, 1981) & Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) with-the-flux auxin canalization, Sachs wound bypass regeneration, and open vs closed leaf venation loops faithfully reproduces Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands) morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.6/100, audit 2026-10-19-auxin-canalization-leaf-veins-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py; output: docs/media/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_comparison.png; organism: Pisum sativum & Arabidopsis thaliana (dicot leaf lamina & stem vascular strands); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: b1e95723b4cbd5f2bb79b0150dbb4ab3fc046d7542c48fe2c7644bb6175993d9; artifact_sha256: 1c852e279db4322139300c4c678bf8eba07a4b621122c88057d60cc618f7aff7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins_reference.json=55e0f743ada83918..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/leaf_venation_canalization_specimen.jpg=7f67774708f8e952..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/paper_citations.bib=95f1b35cf42a8ae7..., datasets/auxin_canalization_leaf_veins/scout_manifest.json=94a1d6a85fe649c5...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-auxin-canalization-leaf-veins-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Mitchison (1980) Proc. R. Soc. B 207:79-109 facilitated diffusion canalization ODEs dD_ij/dt = alpha*|phi_ij|^p + beta - gamma*D_ij proving that linear feedback (p <= 1) yields diffuse flow whereas quadratic feedback (p = 2) triggers winner-take-all symmetry breaking into 1-cell-wide vascular strands where concentration drops inside the canalized vein (S_vein < S_parenchyma) | Mitchison (1981) Phil. Trans. R. Soc. B 295:461-471 & Sachs (1981) Adv. Bot. Res. 9:151-262 polar auxin transport canalization and C-shaped vascular strand bypass regeneration around a transverse stem incision | Feugier, Mochizuki & Iwasa (2005) J. Theor. Biol. 236:366-375 PIN1 carrier-allocation dynamics comparing open hierarchical branching venation trees against closed-areole reticulate venation loops; reconstructed_in_script: 5-regime feedback exponent sweep p in [0.5, 2.5] and 2D cellular lamina canalization solver verifying diffuse flow at p <= 1.0 (winner flux share 0.5000) vs 1-cell-wide canalized strands at p = 2.0 (winner flux share 0.9950, Pearson r = 1.0000, p = 1.48e-9) and auxin concentration drainage inside the vein (S_vein / S_par = 0.3131 < 1.0) | Sachs (1981) 20x16 cellular epicotyl transverse stem incision wound-bypass simulator reproducing C-shaped lateral deflection (4.0 cells, tortuosity L/L0 = 1.3800, sink flux recovery 0.9852) plus NPA polar auxin transport inhibitor negative control (flux recovery 0.0804) | Feugier et al. (2005) PIN1 carrier-allocated venation topology solver verifying pairwise flux conservation (antisymmetry error < 1e-14) and topological transition from open branching trees (Betti-1 = 0 loops, branch angle 52.0 deg) to closed-areole reticulate networks (Betti-1 = 14 loops, branch angle 56.5 deg) | Automated segmentation of the cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton (`leaf_venation_canalization_specimen.jpg`, primary midrib tracking, secondary vein branching angle 52.93 +- 2.53 deg, and 1843 enclosed polygonal areoles); transfer_boundary: 2D cellular lamina canalization and graph cycle-rank topology mapped to cleared dicot leaf venation skeleton; does_not_claim: 3D mechanical leaf blade expansion coupled to viscoelastic turgor-driven epidermal remodeling]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0065-2296(08)60351-1>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2005.03.017>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rspb.1980.0082>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1981.0081>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1365-313X.2005.02581.x> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.926"^^xsd:double .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/8871db0/1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "1997-mitchison-canalization-auxin-flux.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "8871db0" .
}

